This file exists so the directory does.

The VS Code launch configurations use .banter-dev as their working directory, and VS Code
checks that a cwd exists before it starts anything - so without this, a fresh clone or a
`git clean -xfd` left every one of them failing with "Invalid 'cwd' value" before any Banter
code ran. Nothing else creates it.

Everything else in here is ignored: client settings, agent keys, the SQLite database and the
mesh identity written while debugging. None of it belongs in the repository, and none of it
should ever reach the real profile at %APPDATA%/Banter.
